# Phase 16 hygiene fix: normalize text files to LF in the repository
# regardless of the checking-out machine's `core.autocrlf` setting, so
# Windows/Linux/Mac contributors get byte-identical tracked content for
# source and data files (previously several committed CSV/JSON files
# carried CRLF endings in the git object store itself -- not just a
# working-tree artifact -- which this file and the accompanying index
# renormalization fix; see docs/PRODUCTION_READINESS.md).
#
# `text=auto` lets Git's own content heuristic decide text vs. binary for
# anything not explicitly listed below; `eol=lf` then normalizes any file
# Git treats as text to LF on checkout. Binary artifacts are explicitly
# marked `binary` (a shorthand for `-text -diff -merge`) so they are never
# considered for EOL conversion.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.py text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.jsx text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.csv text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.svg text eol=lf
*.ini text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.example text eol=lf
.gitignore text eol=lf

# Binary artifacts -- never subject to EOL conversion.
*.png binary
*.joblib binary
*.pdf binary
*.npy binary
*.faiss binary
